From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: only rescale decoder power when a bitstream
 buffer is queued

A capture QBUF with no bitstream buffer pending sets max_input_data_size
to 0, which drops the session from the bandwidth total. In a live stream
that happens every frame, so the DDR vote flaps between the floor and the
session's vote and each frame pays two interconnect commits on the QBUF
path.

Rescale on bitstream QBUF only, and drop the session from the totals when
its bitstream queue stops.
---
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vb2.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vb2.c
@@ -244,6 +244,9 @@ void iris_vb2_stop_streaming(struct vb2_queue *q)
 	if (ret)
 		goto exit;
 
+	if (V4L2_TYPE_IS_OUTPUT(q->type))
+		inst->max_input_data_size = 0;
+
 exit:
 	iris_helper_buffers_done(inst, q->type, VB2_BUF_STATE_ERROR);
 	if (ret)
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vdec.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vdec.c
@@ -459,9 +459,9 @@ int iris_vdec_qbuf(struct iris_inst *inst, struct vb2_v4l2_buffer *vbuf)
 						   MAXIMUM_FPS);
 			inst->frame_counter = 0;
 		}
-	}
 
-	iris_scale_power(inst);
+		iris_scale_power(inst);
+	}
 
 	return iris_queue_buffer(inst, buf);
 }
